-- title:
--   Supersingular reduced field as a Drinfeld quotient field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$; let $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in $\mathrm{ssJSet}$), assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and fix $s \in W$. Let $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field over $\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, such that $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$ and algebraically closed residue field, and every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$; let $K_b$ be the trivial intermediate field over $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_b$ the valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, assumed a Henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by some $\varpi_b \ne 0$. Regarding $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the conclusion asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ over $k_0$ and valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ generates $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, $W_0 \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$, $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; for every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion of $A_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, with $B$ contained in $W_0$ (inside $F_0$), with $W_0$ the set of ratios $g/h$, $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$, with $B$ stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, and with the special fibre of $B$ described as follows: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of $\mu_{q+1}(\mathbb F_{q^2})$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ with $|C_s| = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, $\ker \rho = (\varpi_b)$, $\rho$ inducing on $A_b$ the residue map of $A$, every element of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ a ratio of values of $\rho$, the range of $\rho$ equal to the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ in the Drinfeld function field, and $\rho$ intertwining $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ with $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ lying in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$; then for every field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with residue field $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, together with a surjection onto $F_{ss}$ with kernel its maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f$ has a scalar multiple with nonzero residue) whose integers cut out $W_0$ on $F_0$, one has: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta$, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of $\mu_{q+1}(\mathbb F_{q^2})$ with $|C_s| = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e : F_{ss} \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ which carries, for each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of $F_{ss}$ to the action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   This identifies the reduced field of a regular prolongation at a supersingular point of the full-level modular curve with the $C_s$-fixed subfield of the function field of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$ over $\kappa$, equivariantly for the level automorphisms indexed by $\Gamma_0(M')$, by transporting the description already available on an affine chart $B$ whose special fibre is the affine Drinfeld quotient. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_affineChart_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_affineChart_chart) in the construction of the semistable model at level $q$.
